# G082 — Content Management System

*v2. See `cms.md` for prose: five-state content lifecycle (Draft →
InReview → Scheduled → Published → Archived), revisions as append-
only, scheduled publish as time-triggered transition, archived as
frozen-but-restorable, slug as natural key and id as surrogate.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Daily Editorial Automation

[editorial-automation
    IN ORDER TO
        notify editors of articles awaiting review each morning
        tick the CMS every minute to promote Scheduled articles on time
        and archive published articles that crossed their retention window

    @cms <- [cms[load]]

    every day at 09:00
        @in-review <- [cms[by-state {cms: @cms, state: "in_review"}]]
        for @a in @in-review
            [email[notify
                    {to: @a:editor,
                     subject: "Awaiting review",
                     article: @a:slug}]]

    every 1 minute
        @new <- [cms[tick {cms: @cms, now-ms: [clock[now]]}]]
        for @a in @new
            [feed[publish {article: @a}]]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[cms
    load
    save-revision        {cms, slug, body, author, now-ms}
                                                       ;; || archived-frozen
    submit-for-review    {cms, id}                      ;; Draft → InReview
    approve-and-publish  {cms, id, now-ms}              ;; → Published
    schedule-publish     {cms, id, at-ms, now-ms}       ;; → Scheduled
    archive              {cms, id}                       ;; any → Archived
    unarchive            {cms, id}                       ;; Archived → Draft
    revert-to-revision   {cms, id, version}              ;; creates NEW revision
    by-state             {cms, state}
    by-tag               {cms, tag}
    by-author            {cms, author}
    by-slug              {cms, slug}
    tick                 {cms, now-ms}                   ;; time-triggered
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: FSM transitions as `where`-gated verbs

[cms[submit-for-review {cms: @c, id: @id}]
    @article <- @c:articles at @id
        where state is "Draft"
            -> state := "InReview"
        otherwise
            -> #illegal-transition
               ("can't submit-for-review from " + current state)
]

[cms[save-revision {cms: @c, slug: @s, body: @b, ...}]
    @article
        where state is "Archived"
            -> #frozen (archived content is read-only by design)
        otherwise
            -> append {version: next, body: @b, author, now-ms}
               to @article:revisions
]

Five states; specific transitions between specific states. Archived
is the only non-terminal frozen state — visible, restorable via
unarchive, but not editable.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: scheduled publish `where` tick catches the time

[cms[tick {cms: @c, now-ms: @now}]
    IN ORDER TO
        promote every Scheduled article whose target time has passed
        so the state machine has both user-triggered and time-triggered edges

    @c:articles
        where state is "Scheduled"
        and publish-at-ms at most @now
            -> state := "Published"
            -> append to the returned list of just-published articles
]

Mixing user-triggered and time-triggered transitions is natural once
the tick mechanism exists — same as G077's auto-lock. The scheduler
lives inside the CMS because content lifecycle is the CMS's concern.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: revisions append-only, revert adds a new revision

[cms[revert-to-revision {cms: @c, id: @id, version: @v}]
    @article
        where state is not "Archived"
            @old <- @article:revisions at version @v
            append {version: next, body: @old:body,
                     author: "reverter", note: "revert to v" + @v}
            IN ORDER TO
                preserve perfect auditability
                so the history always answers "what did it say on day N"
]

Same discipline as Git: reverts are new commits, not rollbacks.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @c <- [cms[load]]
    [cms[save-revision
          {cms: @c, slug: "hello-world",
           body: "first draft", author: "nathan", now-ms: 1000}]]

    [cms[submit-for-review {cms: @c, id: 0}]]
    -> [cms[by-state {cms: @c, state: "in_review"}]]   ;; -> [0]

    [cms[schedule-publish
          {cms: @c, id: 0, at-ms: 5000, now-ms: 2000}]]

    -> [cms[tick {cms: @c, now-ms: 4000}]]              ;; -> []
    -> [cms[tick {cms: @c, now-ms: 6000}]]              ;; -> [article 0]

    [cms[archive {cms: @c, id: 0}]]
    -> [cms[save-revision
             {cms: @c, slug: "hello-world",
              body: "late edit", author: "nathan", now-ms: 7000}]]
    ;; -> #frozen
]
